 # Application-Specific Extensions
+
+Also called: Domain-Specific 3DGS, Non-Photometric Gaussian Splatting, Geometric 3DGS
+
 ## Overview
-Application-Specific Extensions modify the standard 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) framework to handle non-RGB, non-photometric data or to extract explicit geometry from the implicit volumetric representation [G]. While standard 3DGS optimizes for novel-view synthesis of RGB scenes using calibrated camera poses and photometric losses, these adaptations replace the projection target with volumetric supervision, voxel-space rasterization, or 3D geometric intersections [G]. They solve the problem of reconstructing and visualizing high-dimensional or physically distinct data fields where traditional camera-based rendering is inapplicable or insufficient [G].
+Application-Specific Extensions adapt the standard 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) framework [2812-3d-gaussian-splatting.md] to non-photometric domains, explicit geometry extraction, or specialized physical phenomena. While standard 3DGS optimizes for novel-view synthesis of RGB images using view-dependent spherical harmonics, these extensions replace or augment the appearance model with view-independent scalar attributes, geometric priors, or physical quantities. They solve problems such as X-ray tomography, volumetric microscopy, ultrasound imaging, and explicit mesh extraction, where the target data is not surface reflectance but density, distance, or semantic structure.
 
 ## Shared principles
-All extensions in this family retain the core 3DGS primitive representation: a set of $M$ anisotropic 3D Gaussian kernels $\mathcal{G} = \{G_i\}_{i=1}^M$ [G]. Each kernel is defined by:
-*   $\mathbf{p}_i \in \mathbb{R}^3$: Position (mean) [G].
-*   $\mathbf{R}_i \in \mathbb{R}^{3 \times 3}$: Rotation matrix [G].
-*   $\mathbf{S}_i \in \mathbb{R}^{3 \times 3}$: Scale matrix [G].
-*   The covariance matrix is $\mathbf{\Sigma}_i = \mathbf{R}_i \mathbf{S}_i \mathbf{S}_i^\top \mathbf{R}_i^\top$ [G].
